ust so  there's all this kind of so there's the  mystery in this is like way more potent  i think uh than the one that was in  fifth hearts which i think which is why  i liked this one so much more just the  atmosphere of this one is just fantastic  and i'm really really glad that i reread  it  the second time but yeah if that sounds  like something you would like like i  said it's a commitment uh it's very very  very long  um i actually i'm recording this review  like literally like an hour or two  before i have to like put it up because  um i was just like i i spent like all  day reading because it i don't think it  took me that long to read the first time  but i was just kind of like i guess  because i was busy and i just kept you  know having to come back to it and so it  took me like way longer than it normally  would like to read it but yeah it's  super long um but if that sounds like  something you would like and if you like  dan simmons other stuff particularly his  historical fiction um i think this is uh  this is like my favorite historical  fiction of his that i read i think of i  can't remember  i've read like some a bunch of his other  ones that i think were uh really good  too like carrying comfort is really good  and all his other kind of stuff too but  yeah definitely check out drewd like i  said hopefully hopefully one day uh  guillermo del toro  del toro if i could say his [ __ ] name  um we'll  get to make the movie out of it because  i just think that would be  uh fantastic but it seems like such a  long time that i feel like it's probably  not gonna happen now but i'm still kind  of hoping  maybe someday but uh yeah so definitely  check out drewd if it sounds like it's  your cup of tea or your glass of opium  as the case may be and i will see you  guys on the next tomes of terror bye

